  "scope": "Prepared Seq/All restore_in_scope entries borrow an existing LocalExecutionScope and delegate to the original reply cores. Closed scope precedes shape/equality/admission. Structural or native refusal and escaping equality/admission unwind close before retained rows and unused-hook cleanup. Equality/admission revocation wins over duplicate/success/error and stops later hooks; superseded errors drop after closure, while ordinary native errors retain their original owner. Actual live snapshots cover all seven Seq frontiers and eight All masks on numeric/text hosts. Eight new integration tests verify exact original request/reply pointers, unchanged fuel, original native errors, callback/refusal/cleanup unwind and observed once-only retained cleanup after revocation. Legacy unscoped restoration remains unchanged. Successful collectors do not store the scope; later operations and external cancellation remain host responsibilities. Callback-internal native cleanup is not fenced retroactively. No production codec, transaction, crash settlement or complete extraction claim is added.",
